From 9e6430aaf3225d6e16ec4dbad20f4cdc3d0f8a01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pierre Kisters <pierrekisters@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:39:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(java): import_file takes loader, loader_args,
 program_name, analysis_options, if_exists, wait

A raw firmware image needs a load address, a DOS .COM needs BinaryLoader
at 1000:0100, an MZ executable needs MzLoader, and a client could ask for
none of that: import_file auto-detected the format or, given a language,
imported a raw binary at address 0. These are the options AnalyzeHeadless
takes.

- loader ("" as before, "auto", or a loader class name), loader_args
  (-loader-<name>), program_name, analysis_options (set before
  auto-analysis, unknown names refuse and remove the import) and wait
  (false: analysis continues in the background; /analysis_status reports
  analyzing and import_error). ProgramLoader replaces AutoImporter; the
  destination still goes through ProjectPaths.
- if_exists: reuse (default), error or unique. A same-named program is
  now reused only when its recorded SHA-256 matches the file's; opening
  another binary under the requested name answered every later question
  about the wrong program.
- Imports are serialized per destination folder and name. Two clients
  importing one new file at once left a second program called <name>.0.
- A program imported under another name is found by that name.
- Bridge: import_file exposes the parameters and waits up to 1800 s (was
  300) for the analysis a wait=true import covers.

Tests: ImportRequestTest, three ProjectProgramProviderTest cases for the
reuse rule, ProgramImportGhidraTest (real loaders: BinaryLoader at
1000:0100, same bytes, unique, analysis options, wait=false, four
concurrent imports) and the bridge's payload and poll tests.
tests/endpoints.json edited by hand (no Maven here); the generators
report nothing to change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
