diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 841a9fb..1edc843 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -8,6 +8,39 @@ Complete version history for the Ghidra MCP Server project.
 
 Changes on `dev` after 7.0.0.
 
+### Added — `import_file` takes the loader options AnalyzeHeadless takes
+
+A raw firmware image needs a load address, a DOS `.COM` needs `BinaryLoader` at `1000:0100`, an
+MZ executable needs `MzLoader` and a language only as a hint, and a client could ask for none of
+that: `import_file` auto-detected the format, or, given a `language`, imported a raw binary at
+address 0. New parameters, all optional (`ProgramLoader` replaces `AutoImporter`):
+
+- `loader`: `""` (as before: auto-detect, or `BinaryLoader` when a `language` is given), `"auto"`
+  (auto-detect, `language`/`compiler_spec` as hints) or a loader class name such as `MzLoader`.
+- `loader_args`: loader options by name, with or without the `-loader-` prefix
+  (`{"baseAddr": "0x8000"}`).
+- `program_name`: the new program's name in the project (default: the file name). A program
+  imported under another name is found by that name, though the loader names it after the file.
+- `analysis_options`: analyzer options set before auto-analysis, by name; an unknown name or a
+  value that does not parse refuses the call and removes the import again.
+- `if_exists`: `reuse` (default), `error` or `unique` (`name.1`, `name.2`, ...).
+- `wait`: `false` returns once the program is imported and saved; analysis continues in the
+  background, `/analysis_status` reports `analyzing` and, if it did not finish, `import_error`.
+
+Imports are serialized per destination folder and name: two clients importing one new file at
+once used to leave a second program called `<name>.0`; the second now reuses the first's. The
+bridge's `import_file` tool exposes the new parameters (sending only those that differ from the
+defaults) and waits up to 1800 s (was 300) for the analysis a `wait=true` import covers.
+
+### Changed — `import_file` reuses a same-named program only when it holds the same bytes
+
+A program of that name already in the folder was opened and reported as the import
+(`reused_existing: true`), whatever it held, so importing a different build of `D2Common.dll`
+under the same name answered every later question about the old one. It is now reused only when
+its recorded SHA-256 matches the file's (a program that records none is reused as before); other
+bytes are refused with a message that names `if_exists=unique`, another `program_name` or another
+folder.
+
 ### Performance — `get_functions` opens one decompiler per call (#575)
 
 Every decompile in a `get_functions` call -- each target and each caller decompiled for
